{
  "title": "23: Al-Mu'minun المؤمنون",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nقَدْ اَفْلَحَ الْمُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ‏(1)\nQAD AFLAHAL MOAMENOON.\nCertainly, the faithful have attained salvation\nالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ فِىْ صَلَاتِهِمْ خَاشِعُوْنَ ۙ‏(2)\nLAZEENA HUM FEE SALAATEHIM KHAASHE-O’ON.\n—those who are humble in their prayers,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ عَنِ اللَّغْوِ مُعْرِضُوْنَۙ‏(3)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM A’NIL LAGHWE MO’REZOON.\navoid vain talk,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِلزَّكٰوةِ فَاعِلُوْنَۙ‏(4)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM LIZ-ZAKAATE FAA-E’LOON.\ncarry out their [duty of] zakat,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِفُرُوْجِهِمْ حٰفِظُوْنَۙ‏(5)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM LE-FOROOJEHIM HAAFEZOON.\nguard their private parts,\nاِلَّا عَلٰٓى اَزْوَاجِهِمْ اَوْ مَا مَلَكَتْ اَيْمَانُهُمْ فَاِنَّهُمْ غَيْرُ مَلُوْمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(6)\nILLAA A’LAA AZWAAJEHIM AW MAA MALAKAT AYMAANOHUM FA-INNAHUM GHAYRO MALOOMEEN.\n(except from their spouses or their slave women, for then they are not blameworthy;\nفَمَنِ ابْتَغٰى وَرَآءَ ذٰ لِكَ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْعٰدُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(7)\nFAMANIB TAGHAA WARAAA-A ZAALEKA FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL A’ADOON.\nbut whoever seeks [anything] beyond that—it is they who are transgressors),\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ لِاَمٰنٰتِهِمْ وَعَهْدِهِمْ رَاعُوْنَ ۙ‏(8)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM LE-AMAANAATEHIM WA A’HDEHIM RAA-O’ON.\nand those who keep their trusts and covenants\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ عَلٰى صَلَوٰتِهِمْ يُحَافِظُوْنَ‌ۘ‏(9)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM A’LAA SALAWAATEHIM YOHAAFEZOON.\nand are watchful of their prayers.\nاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْوَارِثُوْنَ ۙ‏(10)\nOOLAAA-EKA HOMUL WAARESOON.\nIt is they who will be the inheritors,\nالَّذِيْنَ يَرِثُوْنَ الْفِرْدَوْسَؕ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(11)\nLAZEENA YARESOONAL FIRDAWS, HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nwho shall inherit paradise and will remain in it [forever].\nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ مِنْ سُلٰلَةٍ مِّنْ طِيْنٍ‌ ۚ‏(12)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAL INSAANA MIN SOLAALATIM MIN TEEN.\nCertainly We created man from an extract of clay.\nثُمَّ جَعَلْنٰهُ نُطْفَةً فِىْ قَرَارٍ مَّكِيْنٍ‏(13)\nSUMMA JA-A’LNAAHO NUTFATAN FEE QARAARIM MAKEEN.\nThen We made him a drop of [seminal] fluid [lodged] in a secure abode.\nثُمَّ خَلَقْنَا النُّطْفَةَ عَلَقَةً فَخَلَقْنَا الْعَلَقَةَ مُضْغَةً فَخَلَقْنَا الْمُضْغَةَ عِظٰمًا فَكَسَوْنَا الْعِظٰمَ لَحْمًا ثُمَّ اَنْشَاْنٰهُ خَلْقًا اٰخَرَ‌ ؕ فَتَبٰرَكَ اللّٰهُ اَحْسَنُ الْخٰلِقِيْنَ ؕ‏(14)\nSUMMA KHALAQNAN NUTFATA A’LAQATAN FA-KHALAQNAL A’LAQATA MUZGHATAN FA-KHALAQNAL MUZGHATA E’ZAAMAN FA-KASAWNAL E’ZAAMA LAHMAA, SUMMA ANSHAANAAHO KHALQAN AAKHAR, FA-TABAARAKAL LAAHO AHSANUL KHAALEQEEN.\nThen We created the drop of fluid as a clinging mass. Then We created the clinging mass as a fleshy tissue. Then We created the fleshy tissue as bones. Then We clothed the bones with flesh. Then We produced him as [yet] another creature. So blessed is Allah, the best of creators!\nثُمَّ اِنَّكُمْ بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ لَمَيِّتُوْنَؕ‏(15)\nSUMMA INNAKUM BA’DA ZAALEKA LA-MAYYETOON.\nThen indeed you die after that.\nثُمَّ اِنَّكُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ تُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(16)\nSUMMA INNAKUM YAWMAL QEYAAMATE TUB-A’SOON.\nThen you will indeed be raised up on the Day of Resurrection.\nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا فَوْقَكُمْ سَبْعَ طَرَآئِقَ ۖ  وَمَا كُنَّا عَنِ الْخَلْقِ غٰفِلِيْنَ‏(17)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAA FAWQAKUM SAB-A’ TARAAA-EQ, WA MAA KUNNAA A’NIL KHALQE GHAAFELEEN.\nCertainly We created above you seven levels and We have not been oblivious of the creation.\nوَاَنْزَلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءًۢ بِقَدَرٍ فَاَسْكَنّٰهُ فِى الْاَرْضِ‌ۖ وَاِنَّا عَلٰى ذَهَابٍۢ بِهٖ لَقٰدِرُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(18)\nWA ANZALNAA MENAS SAMAAA-E MAAA-AM BE-QADARIN FA-ASKANNAAHO FIL ARZ, WA INNAA A’LAA ZAHAABIM BEHI LA-QAADEROON.\nWe sent down water from the sky in a measured manner, and We lodged it within the ground, and We are indeed able to take it away.\nفَاَنْشَاْنَا لَكُمْ بِهٖ جَنّٰتٍ مِّنْ نَّخِيْلٍ وَّ اَعْنَابٍ‌ ۘ لَكُمْ فِيْهَا فَوَاكِهُ كَثِيْرَةٌ وَّمِنْهَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ ۙ‏(19)\nFA-ANSHAANAA LAKUM BEHI JANNAATIM MIN NAKHEELINW WA A-A’NAAB, LAKUM FEEHAA FAWAAKEHO KASEERATUNW WA MINHAA TAAKOLOON.\nThen with it We produced for you gardens of date palms and vines. There are abundant fruits in them for you, and you eat from them,\nوَشَجَرَةً تَخْرُجُ مِنْ طُوْرِ سَيْنَآءَ تَنْۢبُتُ بِالدُّهْنِ وَصِبْغٍ لِّلْاٰكِلِيْنَ‏(20)\nWA SHAJARATAN TAKHROJO MIN TOORE SAYNAAA-A TAMBOTO BID-DOHNE WA SIBGHIL LIL-AAKELEEN.\nand a tree that grows on Mount Sinai, which produces oil and a seasoning for those who eat.\nوَ اِنَّ لَكُمْ فِى الْاَنْعَامِ لَعِبْرَةً‌   ؕ نُسْقِيْكُمْ مِّمَّا فِىْ بُطُوْنِهَا وَلَكُمْ فِيْهَا مَنَافِعُ كَثِيْرَةٌ وَّمِنْهَا تَاْكُلُوْنَ ۙ‏(21)\nWA INNA LAKUM FIL AN-A’AME LA-I’BRAH, NUSQEEKUM MIMMAA FEE BOTOONEHAA WA LAKUM FEEHAA MANAAFE-O’ KASEERATUNW WA MINHAA TAAKOLOON.\nThere is indeed a moral for you in the cattle: We give you to drink of that which is in their bellies, and you have many uses in them, and you eat some of them,\nوَعَلَيْهَا وَعَلَى الْفُلْكِ تُحْمَلُوْنَ‏(22)\nWA A’LAYHAA WA A’LAL FULKE TOHMALOON.\nand you are carried on them and on ships.\nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا نُوْحًا اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖ فَقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ اَفَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(23)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA NOOHAN ELAA QAWMEHI FA-QAALA YAA QAWME’BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYROH, AFALAA TATTAQOON.\nCertainly We sent Noah to his people, and he said, ‘O my people! Worship Allah! You have no other god besides Him. Will you not then be wary [of Him]?’\nفَقَالَ الْمَلَؤُا الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ قَوْمِهٖ مَا هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ ۙ يُرِيْدُ اَنْ يَّتَفَضَّلَ عَلَيْكُمْ ؕ وَلَوْ شَآءَ اللّٰهُ لَاَنْزَلَ مَلٰٓئِكَةً  ۖۚ مَّا سَمِعْنَا بِهٰذَا فِىْۤ اٰبَآئِنَا الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‌ ۚ‏(24)\nFA-QAALAL MALA-UL LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN QAWMEHI MAA HAAZAA ILLAA BASHARUM MISLOKUM, YOREEDO AN-Y YATAFAZZALA A’LAYKUM, WA LAW SHAAA-AL LAAHO LA-ANZALA MALAAA-EKAH, MAA SAME’NAA BEHAAZAA FEE AABAAA-ENAL AWWALEEN.\nBut the elite of the faithless from among his people said, ‘This is just a human being like you, who seeks to dominate you. Had Allah wished, He would have sent down angels. We never heard of such a thing among our forefathers.\nاِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا رَجُلٌۢ بِهٖ جِنَّةٌ فَتَرَبَّصُوْا بِهٖ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍ‏(25)\nIN HOWA ILLAA RAJOLUM BEHI JINNATUN FA-TARABBASOO BEHI HATTAA HEEN.\nHe is just a man possessed by madness. So bear with him for a while.’\nقَالَ رَبِّ انْصُرْنِىْ بِمَا كَذَّبُوْنِ‏(26)\nQAALA RABBIN SURNEE BEMAA KAZZABOON.\nHe said, ‘My Lord! Help me, for they impugn me.’\nفَاَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِ اَنِ اصْنَعِ الْفُلْكَ بِاَعْيُنِنَا وَ وَحْيِنَا فَاِذَا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا وَفَارَ التَّنُّوْرُ‌ۙ فَاسْلُكْ فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلٍّ زَوْجَيْنِ اثْنَيْنِ وَاَهْلَكَ اِلَّا مَنْ سَبَقَ عَلَيْهِ الْقَوْلُ مِنْهُمْ‌ۚ وَلَا تُخَاطِبْنِىْ فِى الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا‌ۚ اِنَّهُمْ مُّغْرَقُوْنَ‏(27)\nFA-AWHAYNAA ELAYHE ANIS NA-I’L FULKA BE-A-A’YONENAA WA WAHYENAA FA-EZAA JAAA-A AMRONAA WA FAARAT TANNOORO, FASLUK FEEHAA MIN KULLIN ZAWJAYNIS NAYNE WA AHLAKA ILLAA MAN SABAQA A’LAYHIL QAWLO MINHUM, WA LAA TOKHAATIBNEE FIL LAZEENA ZALAMOO, INNAHUM MUGHRAQOON.\nSo We revealed to him: ‘Build the ark before Our eyes and by Our revelation. When Our edict comes and the oven gushes [a stream of water], bring into it a pair of every kind [of animal], and your family, except those of them against whom the decree has gone beforehand, and do not plead with Me for those who are wrongdoers: they shall indeed be drowned.’\nفَاِذَا اسْتَوَيْتَ اَنْتَ وَمَنْ مَّعَكَ عَلَى الْفُلْكِ فَقُلِ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ نَجّٰٮنَا مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(28)\nFA-EZAS TAWAYTA ANTA WA MAM MA-A’KA A’LAL FULKE FA-QOLIL HAMDO LILLAAHIL LAZEE NAJJAANAA MENAL QAWMIZ ZAALEMEEN.\n‘When you, and those who are with you, are settled in the ark, say, ‘‘All praise belongs to Allah, who has delivered us from the wrongdoing lot.’’\nوَقُلْ رَّبِّ اَنْزِلْنِىْ مُنْزَلًا مُّبٰرَكًا وَّاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الْمُنْزِلِيْنَ‏(29)\nWA QUR RABBE ANZILNEE MUNZALAM MOBAARAKANW WA ANTA KHAYRUL MUNZELEEN.\nAnd say, ‘‘My Lord! Land me with a blessed landing, for You are the best of those who bring ashore.’’ ’\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ وَّاِنْ كُنَّا لَمُبْتَلِيْنَ‏(30)\nINNA FEE ZAALEKA LA-AAYAATINW WA IN KUNNAA LA-MUBTALEEN.\nThere are indeed signs in this; and indeed, We have been testing.\nثُمَّ اَنْشَاْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ قَرْنًا اٰخَرِيْنَ‌ ۚ‏(31)\nSUMMA ANSHAANAA MIM BA’DEHIM QARNAN AAKHAREEN.\nThen after them We brought forth another generation,\nفَاَرْسَلْنَا فِيْهِمْ رَسُوْلًا مِّنْهُمْ اَنِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ‌ ؕ اَفَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(32)\nFA-ARSALNAA FEEHIM RASOOLAM MINHUM ANE’BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYROH, AFALAA TATTAQOON.\nand We sent them an apostle from among themselves, saying, ‘Worship Allah! You have no other god besides Him. Will you not then be wary [of Him]?’\nوَقَالَ الْمَلَاُ مِنْ قَوْمِهِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا وَكَذَّبُوْا بِلِقَآءِ الْاٰخِرَةِ وَاَتْرَفْنٰهُمْ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ۙ مَا هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا بَشَرٌ مِّثْلُكُمْ ۙ يَاْكُلُ مِمَّا تَاْكُلُوْنَ مِنْهُ وَيَشْرَبُ مِمَّا تَشْرَبُوْنَ ۙ‏(33)\nWA QAALAL MALA-O MIN QAWMEHIL LAZEENA KAFAROO WA KAZZABOO BE-LEQAAA-IL AAKHERATE WA ATRAFNAAHUM FIL HAYAATID DUNYAA, MAA HAAZAA ILLAA BASHARUM MISLOKUM, YAAKOLO MIMMAA TAAKOLOONA MINHO WA YASHRABO MIMMAA TASHRABOON.\nSaid the elite of his people, who were faithless and who denied the encounter of the Hereafter and whom We had given affluence in the life of the world: ‘This is just a human being like yourselves: he eats what you eat, and drinks what you drink.\nوَلَئِنْ اَطَعْتُمْ بَشَرًا مِّثْلَكُمْ اِنَّكُمْ اِذًا لَّخٰسِرُوْنَۙ‏(34)\nWA LA-IN ATA’TUM BASHARAM MISLAKUM INNAKUM EZAL LA-KHAASEROON.\nIf you obey a human being like yourselves, you will indeed be losers.\nاَيَعِدُكُمْ اَنَّكُمْ اِذَا مِتُّمْ وَكُنْتُمْ تُرَابًا وَّعِظَامًا اَنَّكُمْ مُّخْرَجُوْنَ ۙ‏(35)\nAYA-E’DOKUM ANNAKUM EZAA MITTUM WA KUNTUM TORAABANW WA E’ZAAMAN ANNAKUM MUKHRAJOON.\nDoes he promise you that when you have died and become bones and dust you will indeed be raised [from the dead]?\nهَيْهَاتَ هَيْهَاتَ لِمَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ ۙ‏(36)\nHAYHAATA HAYHAATA LEMAA TOO-A’DOON.\nFar-fetched, far-fetched is what you are promised!\nاِنْ هِىَ اِلَّا حَيَاتُنَا الدُّنْيَا نَمُوْتُ وَنَحْيَا وَمَا نَحْنُ بِمَبْعُوْثِيْنَ ۙ‏(37)\nIN HEYA ILLAA HAYAATONAD DUNYAA NAMOOTO WA NAHYAA WA MAA NAHNO BE-MAB-O’OSEEN.\nThere is nothing but the life of this world: we live and die, and we will not be resurrected.\nاِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا رَجُلُ اۨفْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا وَّمَا نَحْنُ لَهٗ بِمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(38)\nIN HOWA ILLAA RAJOLONIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBANW WA MAA NAHNO LAHU BE-MOAMENEEN.\nHe is just a man who has fabricated a lie against Allah, and we will not believe in him.’\nقَالَ رَبِّ انْصُرْنِىْ بِمَا كَذَّبُوْنِ‏(39)\nQAALA RABBIN SURNEE BEMAA KAZZABOON.\nHe said, ‘My Lord! Help me, for they impugn me.’\nقَالَ عَمَّا قَلِيْلٍ لَّيُصْبِحُنَّ نٰدِمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(40)\nQAALA A’MMAA QALEELIL LAYUSBEHUNNA NAADEMEEN.\nSaid He, ‘In a little while they will become regretful.’\nفَاَخَذَتْهُمُ الصَّيْحَةُ بِالْحَقِّ فَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ غُثَآءً‌ۚ فَبُعْدًا لِّلْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(41)\nFA-AKHAZATHOMUS SAYHATO BIL-HAQQE FA-JA-A’LNAAHUM GHOSAAA-AA, FA-BO’DAL LIL-QAWMIZ ZAALEMEEN.\nSo the Cry seized them justly and We turned them into a scum. So away with the wrongdoing lot!\nثُمَّ اَنْشَاْنَا مِنْۢ بَعْدِهِمْ قُرُوْنًا اٰخَرِيْنَؕ‏(42)\nSUMMA ANSHAANAA MIM BA’DEHIM QOROONAN AAKHAREEN.\nThen after them We brought forth other generations.\nمَا تَسْبِقُ مِنْ اُمَّةٍ اَجَلَهَا وَمَا يَسْتَاْخِرُوْنَؕ‏(43)\nMAA TASBEQO MIN UMMATIN AJALAHAA WA MAA YASTAAKHEROON.\nNo nation can advance its time nor can it defer it.\nثُمَّ اَرْسَلْنَا رُسُلَنَا تَتْرَا‌ ؕ كُلَّ مَا جَآءَ اُمَّةً رَّسُوْلُهَا كَذَّبُوْهُ‌ فَاَتْبَعْنَا بَعْضَهُمْ بَعْضًا وَّجَعَلْنٰهُمْ اَحَادِيْثَ‌ ۚ فَبُعْدًا لِّقَوْمٍ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(44)\nSUMMA ARSALNAA ROSOLANAA TATRAA, KULLA MAA JAAA-A UMMATAR RASOOLOHAA KAZZABOOHO FA-ATBA’NAA BA’ZAHUM BA’ZANW WA JA-A’LNAAHUM AHAADEES, FA-BO’DAL LE-QAWMIL LAA YOAMENOON.\nThen We sent Our apostles successively. Whenever there came to a nation its apostle, they impugned him, so We made them follow one another [to extinction] and We turned them into folktales. So away with the faithless lot!\nثُمَّ اَرْسَلْنَا مُوْسٰى وَاَخَاهُ هٰرُوْنَ ۙ بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(45)\nSUMMA ARSALNAA MOOSAA WA AKHAAHO HAAROONA, BE-AAYAATENAA WA SULTAANIM MOBEEN.\nThen We sent Moses and Aaron, his brother, with Our signs and a manifest authority\nاِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَا۟ئِهٖ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوْا وَكَانُوْا قَوْمًا عٰلِيْنَ‌ ۚ‏(46)\nELAA FIR-A’WNA WA MALA-EHI FASTAKBAROO WA KAANOO QAWMAN A’ALEEN.\nto Pharaoh and his elites; but they acted arrogantly and they were a tyrannical lot.\nفَقَالُوْۤا اَنُؤْمِنُ لِبَشَرَيْنِ مِثْلِنَا وَقَوْمُهُمَا لَنَا عٰبِدُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(47)\nFA-QAALOO ANOAMENO LE-BASHARAYNE MISLENAA WA QAWMOHOMAA LANAA A’ABEDOON.\nThey said, ‘Shall we believe two humans like ourselves, while their people are our slaves?’\nفَكَذَّبُوْهُمَا فَكَانُوْا مِنَ الْمُهْلَكِيْنَ‏(48)\nFA-KAZZABOOHOMAA FA-KAANOO MENAL MOHLAKEEN.\nSo they impugned the two of them, whereat they were among those who were destroyed.\nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَهْتَدُوْنَ‏(49)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA LA-A’LLAHUM YAHTADOON.\nCertainly We gave Moses the Book so that they might be guided,\nوَجَعَلْنَا ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ وَاُمَّهٗۤ اٰيَةً وَّاٰوَيْنٰهُمَاۤ اِلٰى رَبْوَةٍ ذَاتِ قَرَارٍ وَّمَعِيْنٍ‏(50)\nWA JA-A’LNAB NA MARYAMA WA UMMAHU AAYATANW WA AAWAYNAAHOMAA ELAA RABWATIN ZAATE QARAARINW WA MA-E’EN.\nand We made the son of Mary and his mother a sign, and sheltered them in a level highland with flowing water.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الرُّسُلُ كُلُوْا مِنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ وَاعْمَلُوْا صَالِحًا‌ ؕ اِنِّىْ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ عَلِيْمٌ ؕ‏(51)\nYAA AYYOHAR ROSOLO KOLOO MENAT TAYYEBAATE WA’MALOO SAALEHAA, INNEE BEMAA TA’MALOONA A’LEEM.\nO apostles! Eat of the good things and act righteously. Indeed I know best what you do.\nوَاِنَّ هٰذِهٖۤ اُمَّتُكُمْ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً وَّاَنَا رَبُّكُمْ فَاتَّقُوْنِ‏(52)\nWA INNA HAAZEHI UMMATOKUM UMMATANW WAAHEDATANW WA ANAA RABBOKUM FAT-TAQOON.\nIndeed this community of yours is one community, and I am your Lord, so be wary of Me.\nفَتَقَطَّعُوْۤا اَمْرَهُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ زُبُرًا‌ ؕ كُلُّ حِزْبٍۢ بِمَا لَدَيْهِمْ فَرِحُوْنَ‏(53)\nFA-TAQATTA-O’O AMRAHUM BAYNAHUM ZOBORAA, KULLO HIZBIM BEMAA LADAYHIM FAREHOON.\nBut they fragmented their religion among themselves, each party boasting about what it had.\nفَذَرْهُمْ فِىْ غَمْرَتِهِمْ حَتّٰى حِيْنٍ‏(54)\nFA-ZARHUM FEE GHAMRATEHIM HATTAA HEEN.\nSo leave them in their stupor for a while.\nاَيَحْسَبُوْنَ اَنَّمَا نُمِدُّهُمْ بِهٖ مِنْ مَّالٍ وَّبَنِيْنَۙ‏(55)\nAYAHSABOONA ANNAMAA NOMIDDOHUM BEHI MIM MAALINW WA BANEEN.\nDo they suppose that whatever aid We provide them in regard to wealth and children [is because]\nنُسَارِعُ لَهُمْ فِى الْخَيْرٰتِ‌ ؕ بَلْ لَّا يَشْعُرُوْنَ‏(56)\nNOSAARE-O’ LAHUM FIL KHAYRAAT, BAL LAA YASH-O’ROON.\nWe are eager to bring them good? No, they are not aware!\nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ هُمْ مِّنْ خَشْيَةِ رَبِّهِمْ مُّشْفِقُوْنَۙ‏(57)\nINNAL LAZEENA HUM MIN KHASHYATE RABBEHIM MUSHFEQOON.\nIndeed those who are apprehensive for the fear of their Lord,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ يُؤْمِنُوْنَۙ‏(58)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM BE-AAYAATE RABBEHIM YOAMENOON.\nand believe in the signs of their Lord,\nوَالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ بِرَبِّهِمْ لَا يُشْرِكُوْنَۙ‏(59)\nWAL LAZEENA HUM BE-RABBEHIM LAA YUSHREKOON.\nand do not ascribe partners to their Lord;\nوَالَّذِيْنَ يُؤْتُوْنَ مَاۤ اٰتَوْا وَّ قُلُوْبُهُمْ وَجِلَةٌ اَنَّهُمْ اِلٰى رَبِّهِمْ رٰجِعُوْنَ ۙ‏(60)\nWAL LAZEENA YOATOONA MAA AATAW WA QOLOOBOHUM WAJELATUN ANNAHUM ELAA RABBEHIM RAAJE-O’ON.\nwho give whatever they give while their hearts tremble with awe that they are going to return to their Lord\nاُولٰٓئِكَ يُسَارِعُوْنَ فِىْ الْخَيْرٰتِ وَهُمْ لَهَا سٰبِقُوْنَ‏(61)\nOOLAAA-EKA YOSAARE-O’ONA FIL KHAYRAATE WA HUM LAHAA SAABEQOON.\n—it is they who are zealous in [performing] good works and take the lead in them.\nوَلَا نُكَلِّفُ نَفْسًا اِلَّا وُسْعَهَا‌ وَلَدَيْنَا كِتٰبٌ يَّنْطِقُ بِالْحَقِّ‌ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(62)\nWA LAA NOKALLEFO NAFSAN ILLAA WUS-A’HAA WA LADAYNAA KETAABUN-Y YANTEQO BIL-HAQQE WA HUM LAA YUZLAMOON.\nWe task no soul except according to its capacity, and with Us is a book that speaks the truth, and they will not be wronged.\nبَلْ قُلُوْبُهُمْ فِىْ غَمْرَةٍ مِّنْ هٰذَا وَلَهُمْ اَعْمَالٌ مِّنْ دُوْنِ ذٰلِكَ هُمْ لَهَا عٰمِلُوْنَ‏(63)\nBAL QOLOOBOHUM FEE GHAMRATIM MIN HAAZAA WA LAHUM A-A’MAALUM MIN DOONE ZAALEKA HUM LAHAA A’AMELOON.\nIndeed, their hearts are in a stupor in regard to this, and there are other deeds besides which they perpetrate.\nحَتّٰۤى اِذَاۤ اَخَذْنَا مُتْرَفِيْهِمْ بِالْعَذَابِ اِذَا هُمْ يَجْئَرُوْنَؕ‏(64)\nHATTAA EZAA AKHAZNAA MUTRAFEEHIM BIL-A’ZAABE EZAA HUM YAJ-AROON.\nWhen We seize their affluent ones with punishment, behold, they make entreaties [to Us].\nلَا تَجْئَرُوا الْيَوْمَ‌ اِنَّكُمْ مِّنَّا لَا تُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(65)\nLAA TAJ-ARUL YAWM, INNAKUM MINNAA LAA TUNSAROON.\n‘Do not make entreaties today! Indeed, you will not receive any help from Us.\nقَدْ كَانَتْ اٰيٰتِىْ تُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ فَكُنْتُمْ عَلٰٓى اَعْقَابِكُمْ تَنْكِصُوْنَۙ‏(66)\nQAD KAANAT AAYAATEE TUTLAA A’LAYKUM FA-KUNTUM A’LAA A-A’QAABEKUM TANKESOON.\nCertainly My signs used to be recited to you, but you used to take to your heels,\nمُسْتَكْبِرِيْنَ ‌ۖ  بِهٖ سٰمِرًا تَهْجُرُوْنَ‏(67)\nMUSTAKBEREEN, BEHI SAAMERAN TAHJOROON.\nbeing disdainful of it, talking nonsense in your nightly sessions.’\nاَفَلَمْ يَدَّبَّرُوا الْقَوْلَ اَمْ جَآءَهُمْ مَّا لَمْ يَاْتِ اٰبَآءَهُمُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(68)\nAFALAM YADDABBARUL QAWLA AM JAAA-AHUM MAA LAM YAATE AABAAA-AHOMUL AWWALEEN.\nHave they not contemplated the Discourse, or has anything come to them [in it] that did not come to their forefathers?\nاَمْ لَمْ يَعْرِفُوْا رَسُوْلَهُمْ فَهُمْ لَهٗ مُنْكِرُوْنَ‏(69)\nAM LAM YA’REFOO RASOOLAHUM FAHUM LAHU MUNKEROON.\nIs it that they do not recognize their apostle, and so they deny him?\nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ بِهٖ جِنَّةٌ  ؕ بَلْ جَآءَهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ وَاَكْثَرُهُمْ لِلْحَقِّ كٰرِهُوْنَ‏(70)\nAM YAQOOLOONA BEHI JINNAH, BAL JAAA-AHUM BIL-HAQQE WA AKSAROHUM LIL-HAQQE KAAREHOON.\nDo they say, ‘There is madness in him’? No, he has brought them the truth, and most of them are averse to the truth.\nوَلَوِ اتَّبَعَ الْحَقُّ اَهْوَآءَهُمْ لَفَسَدَتِ السَّمٰوٰتُ وَالْاَرْضُ وَمَنْ فِيْهِنَّ‌ؕ بَلْ اَتَيْنٰهُمْ بِذِكْرِهِمْ فَهُمْ عَنْ ذِكْرِهِمْ مُّعْرِضُوْنَؕ‏(71)\nWA LAWIT TABA-A’L HAQQO AHWAAA-AHUM LAFASADATIS SAMAAWAATO WAL ARZO WA MAN FEEHIN, BAL ATAYNAAHUM BE-ZIKREHIM FAHUM A’N ZIKREHIM MO’REZOON.\nHad the truth followed their desires, the heavens and the earth would have surely fallen apart [along] with those who are in them. Indeed, We have brought them their Reminder, but they are disregardful of their Reminder.\nاَمْ تَسْئَلُهُمْ خَرْجًا فَخَرٰجُ رَبِّكَ خَيْرٌ‌ ‌ۖ  وَّهُوَ خَيْرُ الرّٰزِقِيْنَ‏(72)\nAM TAS-ALOHUM KHARJAN FA-KHARAAJO RABBEKA KHAYR, WA HOWA KHAYRUR RAAZEQEEN.\nDo you ask a recompense from them? Your Lord’s recompense is better, and He is the best of providers.\nوَاِنَّكَ لَتَدْعُوْهُمْ اِلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(73)\nWA INNAKA LATAD-O’OHUM ELAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\nIndeed you invite them to a straight path,\nوَاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ عَنِ الصِّرَاطِ لَنٰكِبُوْنَ‏(74)\nWA INNAL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL-AAKHERATE A’NIS SERAATE LA-NAAKEBOON.\nand those who do not believe in the Hereafter surely deviate from the path.\nوَلَوْ رَحِمْنٰهُمْ وَكَشَفْنَا مَا بِهِمْ مِّنْ ضُرٍّ لَّلَجُّوْا فِىْ طُغْيَانِهِمْ يَعْمَهُوْنَ‏(75)\nWA LAW RAHIMNAAHUM WA KASHAFNAA MAA BEHIM MIN ZURRIL LALAJJOO FEE TUGHYAANEHIM YA’MAHOON.\nShould We have mercy upon them and remove their distress, they would surely persist, bewildered in their rebellion.\nوَلَقَدْ اَخَذْنٰهُمْ بِالْعَذَابِ فَمَا اسْتَكَانُوْا لِرَبِّهِمْ وَمَا يَتَضَرَّعُوْنَ‏(76)\nWA LAQAD AKHAZNAAHUM BIL-A’ZAABE FAMAS TAKAANOO LE-RABBEHIM WA MAA YATAZARRA-O’ON.\nWe have already seized them with punishment, yet they did not humble themselves before their Lord, nor will they entreat [Him for mercy]\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا فَتَحْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ بَابًا ذَا عَذَابٍ شَدِيْدٍ اِذَا هُمْ فِيْهِ مُبْلِسُوْنَ‏(77)\nHATTAA EZAA FATAHNAA A’LAYHIM BAABAN ZAA A’ZAABIN SHADEEDIN EZAA HUM FEEHE MUBLESOON.\nuntil We open on them the gate of a severe punishment, whereupon they will be despondent in it.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْۤ اَنْشَاَ لَكُمُ السَّمْعَ وَالْاَبْصَارَ وَالْاَفْئِدَةَ‌  ؕ قَلِيْلًا مَّا تَشْكُرُوْنَ‏(78)\nWA HOWAL LAZEE ANSHA-A LAKOMUS SAM-A’ WAL ABSAARA WAL AF-EDAH, QALEELAM MAA TASHKOROON.\nIt is He who made for you hearing, eyesight, and hearts. Little do you thank.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ ذَرَاَكُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَاِلَيْهِ تُحْشَرُوْنَ‏(79)\nWA HOWAL LAZEE ZARA-AKUM FIL ARZE WA ELAYHE TOHSHAROON.\nIt is He who created you on the earth, and you will be mustered toward Him.\nوَهُوَ الَّذِىْ يُحْىٖ وَيُمِيْتُ وَلَهُ اخْتِلَافُ الَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ‌ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(80)\nWA HOWAL LAZEE YOHYEE WA YOMEETO WA LAHUKH TELAAFUL LAYLE WAN NAHAAR, AFALAA TA’QELOON.\nAnd it is He who gives life and brings death, and due to Him is the alternation of day and night. Do you not exercise your reason?\nبَلْ قَالُوْا مِثْلَ مَا قَالَ الْاَوَّلُوْنَ‏(81)\nBAL QAALOO MISLA MAA QAALAL AWWALOON.\nIndeed, they say, just like what the former peoples said.\nقَالُوْۤا ءَاِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا وَّ عِظَامًا ءَاِنَّا لَمَبْعُوْثُوْنَ‏(82)\nQAALOO A-EZAA MITNAA WA KUNNAA TORAABANW WA E’ZAAMAN A-INNAA LA-MAB-O’OSOON.\nThey said, ‘What, when we are dead and become dust and bones, shall we be resurrected?\nلَقَدْ وُعِدْنَا نَحْنُ وَاٰبَآؤُنَا هٰذَا مِنْ قَبْلُ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اَسَاطِيْرُ الْاَوَّلِيْنَ‏(83)\nLAQAD WO-I’DNAA NAHNO WA AABAAA-ONAA HAAZAA MIN QABLO IN HAAZAA ILLAA ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\nCertainly, we and our fathers were promised this before. [But] these are nothing but myths of the ancients.’\nقُلْ لِّمَنِ الْاَرْضُ وَمَنْ فِيْهَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(84)\nQUL LEMANIL ARZO WA MAN FEEHAA IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nSay, ‘To whom does the earth belong and whoever it contains, if you know?’\nسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ لِلّٰهِ‌ؕ قُلْ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(85)\nSAYAQOOLOONA LILLAAH, QUL AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nThey will say, ‘To Allah.’ Say, ‘Will you not then take admonition?’\nقُلْ مَنْ رَّبُّ السَّمٰوٰتِ السَّبْعِ وَرَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيْمِ‏(86)\nQUL MAR RABBUS SAMAAWAATIS SAB-E’ WA RABBUL A’RSHIL A’ZEEM.\nSay, ‘Who is the Lord of the seven heavens and the Lord of the Great Throne?’\nسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ لِلّٰهِ‌ؕ قُلْ اَفَلَا تَتَّقُوْنَ‏(87)\nSAYAQOOLOONA LILLAAH, QUL AFALAA TATTAQOON.\nThey will say, ‘[They belong] to Allah.’ Say, ‘Will you not then be wary [of Him]?’\nقُلْ مَنْۢ بِيَدِهٖ مَلَكُوْتُ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّهُوَ يُجِيْرُ وَلَا يُجَارُ عَلَيْهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(88)\nQUL MAM BE-YADEHI MALAKOOTO KULLE SHAY-INW WA HOWA YOJEERO WA LAA YOJAARO A’LAYHE IN KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nSay, ‘In whose hand is the dominion of all things, and who gives shelter and no shelter can be provided from Him, if you know?’\nسَيَقُوْلُوْنَ لِلّٰهِ‌ؕ قُلْ فَاَنّٰى تُسْحَرُوْنَ‏(89)\nSAYAQOOLOONA LILLAAH, QUL FA-ANNAA TUSHAROON.\nThey will say, ‘[They all belong] to Allah.’ Say, ‘Then how are you so deluded?’\nبَلْ اَتَيْنٰهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ‏(90)\nBAL ATAYNAAHUM BIL-HAQQE WA INNAHUM LA-KAAZEBOON.\nIndeed, We have brought them the truth, and they are indeed liars.\nمَا اتَّخَذَ اللّٰهُ مِنْ وَّلَدٍ وَّمَا كَانَ مَعَهٗ مِنْ اِلٰهٍ‌ اِذًا لَّذَهَبَ كُلُّ اِلٰهٍۢ بِمَا خَلَقَ وَلَعَلَا بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ‌ؕ سُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ عَمَّا يَصِفُوْنَۙ‏(91)\nMAT TAKHAZAL LAAHO MINW WALADINW WA MAA KAANA MA-A’HU MIN ELAAHIN EZAL LAZAHABA KULLO ELAAHIM BEMAA KHALAQA WA LA-A’LAA BA’ZOHUM A’LAA BA’Z, SUBHAANAL LAAHE A’MMAA YASEFOON.\nAllah has not taken any offspring, neither is there any god besides Him, for then each god would take away what he created, and some of them would surely rise up against others. Clear is Allah of what they allege!\nعٰلِمِ الْغَيْبِ وَالشَّهَادَةِ فَتَعٰلٰى عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(92)\nA’ALEMIL GHAYBE WASH SHAHAADATE FA-TA-A’ALAA A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nThe Knower of the sensible and the Unseen, He is above having any partners that they ascribe [to Him].\nقُل رَّبِّ اِمَّا تُرِيَنِّىْ مَا يُوْعَدُوْنَۙ‏(93)\nQUR RABBE IMMAA TOREYANNEE MAA YOO-A’DOON.\nSay, ‘My Lord! If You should show me what they are promised,\nرَبِّ فَلَا تَجْعَلْنِىْ فِى الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(94)\nRABBE FALAA TAJ-A’LNEE FIL QAWMIZ ZAALEMEEN.\nthen do not put me, my Lord, among the wrongdoing lot.’\nوَاِنَّا عَلٰٓى اَنْ نُّرِيَكَ مَا نَعِدُهُمْ لَقٰدِرُوْنَ‏(95)\nWA INNAA A’LAA AN NOREYAKA MAA NA-E’DOHUM LA-QAADEROON.\nWe are indeed able to show you what We promise them.\nاِدْفَعْ بِالَّتِىْ هِىَ اَحْسَنُ السَّيِّئَةَ‌ ؕ نَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَصِفُوْنَ‏(96)\nIDFA’ BILLATEE HEYA AHSANUS SAYYE-AH, NAHNO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YASEFOON.\nRepel ill [conduct] with that which is the best. We know best whatever they allege.\nوَقُلْ رَّبِّ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ مِنْ هَمَزٰتِ الشَّيٰطِيْنِۙ‏(97)\nWA QUR RABBE A-O’OZO BEKA MIN HAMAZAATISH SHAYAATEEN.\nSay, ‘My Lord! I seek Your protection from the promptings of devils,\nوَاَعُوْذُ بِكَ رَبِّ اَنْ يَّحْضُرُوْنِ‏(98)\nWA A-O’OZO BEKA RABBE AN-Y YAHZOROON.\nand I seek Your protection, my Lord, from their presence near me.’\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا جَآءَ اَحَدَهُمُ الْمَوْتُ قَالَ رَبِّ ارْجِعُوْنِۙ‏(99)\nHATTAA EZAA JAAA-A AHADAHOMUL MAWTO QAALA RABBIR JE-O’ON.\nWhen death comes to one of them, he says, ‘My Lord! Take me back,\nلَعَلِّىْۤ اَعْمَلُ صَالِحًا فِيْمَا تَرَكْتُ‌ؕ كَلَّا‌ ؕ اِنَّهَا كَلِمَةٌ هُوَ قَآئِلُهَا‌ؕ وَمِنْ وَّرَآئِهِمْ بَرْزَخٌ اِلٰى يَوْمِ يُبْعَثُوْنَ‏(100)\nLA-A’LLEE A-A’MALO SAALEHAN FEEMAA TARAKT, KALLAA, INNAHAA KALEMATUN HOWA QAAA-ELOHAA, WA MINW WARAAA-EHIM BARZAKHUN ELAA YAWME YUB-A’SOON.\nthat I may act righteously in what I have left behind.’ ‘By no means! These are mere words that he says.’ And before them is a barrier until the day they will be resurrected.\nفَاِذَا نُفِخَ فِى الصُّوْرِ فَلَاۤ اَنْسَابَ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ وَّلَا يَتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(101)\nFA-EZAA NOFEKHA FIS SOORE FALAA ANSAABA BAYNAHUM YAWMA-EZINW WA LAA YATASAAA-ALOON.\nWhen the Trumpet is blown, there will be no ties between them on that day, nor will they ask [about] each other.\nفَمَنْ ثَقُلَتْ مَوَازِيْنُهٗ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ هُمُ الْمُفْلِحُوْنَ‏(102)\nFAMAN SAQOLAT MAWAAZEENOHU FA-OOLAAA-EKA HOMUL MUFLEHOON.\nThen those whose deeds weigh heavy in the scales—it is they who are the felicitous.\nوَمَنْ خَفَّتْ مَوَازِيْنُهٗ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدُوْنَ‌ ۚ‏(103)\nWA MAN KHAFFAT MAWAAZEENOHU FA-OOLAAA-EKAL LAZEENA KHASEROO ANFOSAHUM FEE JAHANNAMA KHAALEDOON.\nAs for those whose deeds weigh light in the scales—they will be the ones who have ruined their souls, and they will remain in hell [forever].\nتَلْفَحُ وُجُوْهَهُمُ النَّارُ وَهُمْ فِيْهَا كٰلِحُوْنَ‏(104)\nTALFAHO WOJOOHAHOMUN NAARO WA HUM FEEHAA KAALEHOON.\nThe Fire will scorch their faces, while they snarl baring their teeth.\nاَلَمْ تَكُنْ اٰيٰتِىْ تُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ فَكُنْتُمْ بِهَا تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(105)\nALAM TAKUN AAYAATEE TUTLAA A’LAYKUM FA-KUNTUM BEHAA TOKAZZEBOON.\n‘Was it not that My signs were recited to you but you would deny them?’\nقَالُوْا رَبَّنَا غَلَبَتْ عَلَيْنَا شِقْوَتُنَا وَكُنَّا قَوْمًا ضَآلِّيْنَ‏(106)\nQAALOO RABBANAA GHALABAT A’LAYNAA SHIQWATONAA WA KUNNAA QAWMAN ZAALLEEN.\nThey will say, ‘Our Lord! Our wretchedness overcame us, and we were an astray lot.\nرَبَّنَاۤ اَخْرِجْنَا مِنْهَا فَاِنْ عُدْنَا فَاِنَّا ظٰلِمُوْنَ‏(107)\nRABBANAA AKHRIJNAA MINHAA FA-IN U’DNAA FA-INNAA ZAALEMOON.\nOur Lord! Bring us out of this! Then, if we revert [to our previous conduct], we will indeed be wrongdoers.’\nقَالَ اخْسَئُوْا فِيْهَا وَلَا تُكَلِّمُوْنِ‏(108)\nQAALAKH SA-OO FEEHAA WA LAA TOKALLEMOON.\nHe will say, ‘Begone in it, and do not speak to Me!\nاِنَّهٗ كَانَ فَرِيْقٌ مِّنْ عِبَادِىْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَاۤ اٰمَنَّا فَاغْفِرْ لَنَا وَارْحَمْنَا وَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ‌‌ۖ‌ۚ‏(109)\nINNAHU KAANA FAREEQUM MIN E’BAADEE YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA AAMANNAA FAGHFIR LANAA WAR HAMNAA WA ANTA KHAYRUR RAAHEMEEN.\nIndeed there was a part of My servants who would say, ‘‘Our Lord! We have believed. So forgive us, and have mercy on us, and You are the best of the merciful.’’\nفَاتَّخَذْتُمُوْهُمْ سِخْرِيًّا حَتّٰٓى اَنْسَوْكُمْ ذِكْرِىْ وَكُنْتُمْ مِّنْهُمْ تَضْحَكُوْنَ‏(110)\nFAT-TAKHAZTOMOOHUM SIKHRIYYAN HATTAA ANSAWKUM ZIKREE WA KUNTUM MINHUM TAZHAKOON.\nBut you took them by ridicule until they made you forget My remembrance, and you used to laugh at them.\nاِنِّىْ جَزَيْتُهُمُ الْيَوْمَ بِمَا صَبَرُوْۤا ۙ اَنَّهُمْ هُمُ الْفَآئِزُوْنَ‏(111)\nINNEE JAZAYTOHOMUL YAWMA BEMAA SABAROO, ANNAHUM HOMUL FAAA-EZOON.\nIndeed I have rewarded them today for their patience. They are indeed the triumphant.’\nقٰلَ كَمْ لَبِثْتُمْ فِى الْاَرْضِ عَدَدَ سِنِيْنَ‏(112)\nQAALA KAM LABISTUM FIL ARZE A’DADA SENEEN.\nHe will say, ‘How many years did you remain on earth?’\nقَالُوْا لَبِثْنَا يَوْمًا اَوْ بَعْضَ يَوْمٍ فَسْئَلِ الْعَآدِّيْنَ‏(113)\nQAALOO LABISNAA YAWMAN AW BA’ZA YAWMIN FAS-ALIL A’ADDEEN.\nThey will say, ‘We remained for a day, or part of a day; yet ask those who keep the count.’\nقٰلَ اِنْ لَّبِثْتُمْ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا لَّوْ اَنَّكُمْ كُنْتُمْ تَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(114)\nQAALA IL LABISTUM ILLAA QALEELAL LAW ANNAKUM KUNTUM TA’LAMOON.\nHe will say, ‘You only remained a little; if only you had known.\nاَفَحَسِبْتُمْ اَنَّمَا خَلَقْنٰكُمْ عَبَثًا وَّاَنَّكُمْ اِلَيْنَا لَا تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(115)\nAFAHASIBTUM ANNAMAA KHALAQNAAKUM A’BASANW WA ANNAKUM ELAYNAA LAA TURJAO’ON. \nDid you suppose that We created you aimlessly, and that you will not be brought back to Us?’\nفَتَعٰلَى اللّٰهُ الْمَلِكُ الْحَقُّ‌ ۚ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ‌ۚ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْكَرِيْمِ‏(116)\nFA-TAA’ALAL LAAHUL MALEKUL HAQQO, LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA RABBUL A’RSHIL KAREEM. \nSo exalted is Allah, the True Sovereign, there is no god except Him, the Lord of the Noble Throne.\nوَمَنْ يَّدْعُ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَۙ لَا بُرْهَانَ لَهٗ بِهٖۙ فَاِنَّمَا حِسَابُهٗ عِنْدَ رَبِّهٖؕ اِنَّهٗ لَا يُفْلِحُ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ‏(117)\nWA MANY YAD-O’ MA-A’LLAAHE ELAAHAN AAKHARA, LAA BURHAANA LAHU BEHI, FA-INNAMAA HESAABOHU I’NDA RABBEHI, INNAHU LAA YUFLEHUL KAAFEROON. \nWhoever invokes besides Allah another god of which he has no proof, his reckoning will indeed rest with his Lord. Indeed the faithless will not be felicitous.\nوَقُلْ رَّبِّ اغْفِرْ وَارْحَمْ وَاَنْتَ خَيْرُ الرّٰحِمِيْنَ‏(118)\nWA QUR RABBIGH FIR WAR HAM WA ANTA KHAYRUR RAAHEMEEN.\nSay, ‘My Lord, forgive and have mercy, and You are the best of the merciful.’",
  "merits": "Surah al-Momenoon (The Believers)\nThis Surah was revealed in Makkah and it has 118 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the reciter of this Surah will feel great comfort when the angel of death comes to take his soul and he will be given the good news of his position by angels.\nIt is narrated from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) that whoever recites this Surah on every Friday, he will have a great status in the hereafter and will be in the company of prophets. If this Surah is written (at night) and put on the neck of a drunkard, he will start hating intoxicating drinks and will stop this bad habit."
